our meetings the African Union and EU  PSC meetings Peace and Security Council  on the African site the political and  security committee on our side are an  extremely useful tool in order to  exchange views yesterday in a more  informal setting we have discussed the  issue of countering terrorism but also  countering radicalization and violent  extremism on the one side and then the  other side also the issue of migration  today we focused on the crisis  situations in Africa namely the  Democratic Republic of Congo the Central  African Republic Somalia Sahel South  Sudan Burundian guinea-bissau then we  had also a conversation on how we could  even further strengthen our cooperation  African Union European Union but also  between our two comedies and the idea of  maybe a joint trip which we have already  undertaken one in in Mali about a year  and a half ago which was extremely  successful so we want to build on that  the retreat did focus on terrorism and  migration two huge concerns for both our  continents and we did come up with  concrete outcomes and a way forward and  how we can work together to deal with  these two situations on the Democratic  Republic of Congo we appraise ourselves  on the situation and agreed that this  country was to be encouraged to hold  elections as quickly as possible on the  Central African Republic we agreed that  we need to remain involved with this  country that is still quite fragile to  ensure that they're able to build  governance and administrative  institutions we also appreciated a need  to support Somalia during this time as  they work towards having elections and  and obviously the issues of state  formation and capacity building within  the Somali National Army which would  then take over from Amazon  on South Sudan we appreciated that South  Sudan had finally accepted the  deployment of the Protection Force we  discussed the possibility of having  joint missions to a crisis situation we  had one in the past O'Malley tha